{
  "name": "C · User notification",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "0c0c0c0c-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -32,
        -448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1360,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## C · User notification\nRuns after Workflow B has written a batch's matches (or manually, for the most recent matched batch). One database round trip when nothing is sent, plus one per email sent.\n1. **Plan notifications** (one SQL statement): read `app_config` and refuse to record anything unless `EMAIL_MODE` is `suppressed` or `test_aliases` and the cap, aliases and sender are valid; record every user with new matches. In `test_aliases` mode the first `EMAIL_CAP` users are `pending` with a test alias as recipient; everyone else is `suppressed`. With nothing pending the batch is closed here. A rerun finds them all recorded and sends nothing.\n2. **Check email settings**: the same checks again in code; stops the workflow with the reason.\n3. **Render emails** for those users only. In `suppressed` mode they are previews and stop here.\n4. **Check recipients**, then one email at a time: send through SES, record the result (the last one closes the batch), pause to stay under the SES rate.\nn8n never holds more than `EMAIL_CAP` emails, and never a user's real address."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0c0c0c0c-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Never the CSV address",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1376,
        -448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1120,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "### Who can receive an email\n* The planning query never selects `users.email`: the address from the upload cannot reach this workflow.\n* Recipients come only from `EMAIL_ALIASES`, and only in `test_aliases` mode.\n* `EMAIL_CAP` is applied twice: in the query (only that many become `pending`) and in **Check recipients**.\n* **Check recipients** stops everything unless every recipient is one of the aliases, used once, and the sender is `SES_SENDER`.\n* The SES credential is a send-only IAM user, never the owner's admin keys; the SES sandbox (verified identities only) is the second layer."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0c0c0c0c-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Called by Workflow B",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
